201
00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:10.910
<v Speaker 2>In a moment of crisis, he substituted his own judgment for the direct command of the prophet.

202
00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:16.110
<v Speaker 1>In stark contrast, the commander of the faithful, peace be upon him, held the field.

203
00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:20.590
<v Speaker 1>He obeyed the explicit command perfectly, remaining steadfast even as others retreated.

204
00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:28.270
<v Speaker 1>The author uses this not merely as a record of military bravery, but as a theological test of the precise quality required of a guide.

