241
00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:59.710
<v Speaker 2>The author treats this pulpit confession as an inescapable logical dilemma.

242
00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:03.790
<v Speaker 2>If we analyze it with cold precision, there are only two possibilities.

243
00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:07.230
<v Speaker 2>The first possibility is that Abu Bakr was telling the truth.

244
00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:15.070
<v Speaker 2>If he was truthful in stating he was not the best, then his later partisans are lying when they claim he was the most excellent member of the community.

245
00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:17.950
<v Speaker 2>They are directly contradicting the man they revere.

246
00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:19.230
<v Speaker 1>Okay, I see the trap there.

247
00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:23.870
<v Speaker 1>Either he was telling the truth, which means his partisans are lying when they claim he is the best,

248
00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:28.270
<v Speaker 1>Or he was lying from the pulpit, and a proven liar cannot possibly be the guide.

249
00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.150
<v Speaker 2>Exactly.

250
00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:32.910
<v Speaker 2>There is no third option that preserves the claim of his superiority.

251
00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:43.870
<v Speaker 2>Some might try to defend this by claiming it was merely the modest self-deprecation of a humble leader, but the author completely rejects this defense by contrasting it with the behavior of true guides.

252
00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:44.990
<v Speaker 1>How so?

253
00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:50.030
<v Speaker 2>Well, the prophet openly stated his rank as the master of the children of Adam without any false modesty.

254
00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:55.150
<v Speaker 2>The commander of the faithful spoke openly of the torrent of knowledge pouring down from him.

255
00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:56.110
<v Speaker 1>I see.

256
00:17:56.590 --> 00:18:01.550
<v Speaker 1>A rightful designated leader states his rank plainly because it's the objective truth.

257
00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:04.910
<v Speaker 2>A public declaration of inferiority is not hidden modesty.

258
00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:08.110
<v Speaker 2>It's an accurate admission of a real absence of designation.

259
00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:12.310
<v Speaker 2>A man who has been designated knows his rank and does not disown it.

260
00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:18.670
<v Speaker 1>The author then drives the final nail into the argument for an election by using Umar's own words against the process.

261
00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:24.790
<v Speaker 1>Umar publicly admitted that the first oath of allegiance given to Abu Bakr was a falta.

262
00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:25.950
