263
00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:28.750
<v Speaker 2>An unconsidered, rushed decision.

264
00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:33.710
<v Speaker 2>Umar explicitly warned against anyone ever attempting to replicate such a chaotic process again.

265
00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:39.550
<v Speaker 2>The author seizes on this admission because it demolishes the central claim of the elected assembly from the inside out.

266
00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:49.030
<v Speaker 1>Yeah, if the succession was truly a divine command, or even the careful execution of the prophet's implicit wishes, it couldn't possibly be described by its architect as a hasty slip.

267
00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.230
<v Speaker 1>A divine appointment is not a scramble.

268
00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:59.230
<v Speaker 2>Umar concedes, by his own account, that the foundational act of their succession was not the considered execution of a divine mandate.

269
00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.990
<v Speaker 2>It was a rushed slip.

270
00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:07.630
<v Speaker 2>The caliph's own words, preserved in their own records, dismantled their claim to rightful authority.

271
00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.710
<v Speaker 2>The author has done nothing more than read their own history back to them.

272
00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:16.030
<v Speaker 1>When we step back and look at the entire scope of this argument, it is remarkable.

273
00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:27.470
<v Speaker 1>the author has taken us through the unbroken line of the prophets, demonstrating that from the angels onward, the earth always has a designated guide, and that guide never comes by human choice.

274
00:19:27.710 --> 00:19:31.950
<v Speaker 2>And he applied that exact principle to render a definitive verdict on history.

275
00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:36.910
<v Speaker 2>He measured the historical figures against the objective virtues of knowledge, holy struggle, and piety.

276
00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:43.830
<v Speaker 2>He found the chosen leaders wanting based on their own admissions, and he pointed to the one man who held all three virtues at their summit.

277
00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:45.830
<v Speaker 1>It all circles back to that terrifying

278
00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:46.990
<v Speaker 1>image of Noah's Ark.

279
00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:48.750
<v Speaker 1>History is a repeating test.

280
00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:51.630
<v Speaker 1>The people who drowned in the flood had the warning.

281
00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.230
<v Speaker 1>They saw the vessel clearly.

282
00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:57.790
<v Speaker 1>Their tragedy was trusting the solid ground beneath their own feet over the designated ship.

283
00:19:58.030 --> 00:20:03.390
<v Speaker 2>The earth is never left without a guide, and that guide comes by designation, never by election.

284
00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.430
<v Speaker 1>So we leave you with this to consider on your own.

285
00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:11.070
<v Speaker 1>When you look at the structure of your own decisions, where do you prefer your own judgment?

286
00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:15.310
